ils":[],"status":"not_checked","observedAt":"2026-09-16T04:12:02.164Z"},{"url":"https://www.instagram.com/adayinthelifeofasaddlefitter","platform":"instagram","identityStatus":"channel_published","associationSourceUrls":["https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChA8TK7yu46RU6bv8TriYhg"],"websites":[],"publicEmails":[],"status":"not_checked","observedAt":"2026-09-16T04:12:02.164Z"},{"url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber","platform":"tiktok","identityStatus":"channel_published","associationSourceUrls":["https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChA8TK7yu46RU6bv8TriYhg"],"websites":[],"publicEmails":[],"status":"collected","observedAt":"2026-09-17T11:19:04.895Z","followers":{"value":7197,"raw":"7197","precision":"exact","sourceUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/embed/@poppywebber?lang=zh-CN&embedFrom=oembed","observedAt":"2026-09-17T11:19:04.895Z"},"following":{"value":93,"raw":"93","precision":"exact","sourceUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/embed/@poppywebber?lang=zh-CN&embedFrom=oembed","observedAt":"2026-09-17T11:19:04.895Z"},"totalLikes":{"value":29900,"raw":"29900","precision":"exact","sourceUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/embed/@poppywebber?lang=zh-CN&embedFrom=oembed","observedAt":"2026-09-17T11:19:04.895Z"},"source":{"kind":"creator_embed","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/embed/@poppywebber?lang=zh-CN&embedFrom=oembed","observedAt":"2026-09-17T11:19:04.895Z","contentHash":"916c0b7f49f0b810e93c6d21d7f5be4b8bb364bc60a5454afe360e77ab202853"},"videoSnapshot":{"sourceUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/embed/@poppywebber?lang=zh-CN&embedFrom=oembed","observedAt":"2026-09-17T11:19:04.895Z","discoveryBasis":"creator_embed","latestVerified":false,"videos":[{"id":"7327769325710871841","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7327769325710871841","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Here’s one reason to use a half pad! Ps lambskin ones rated highest in independent testing - make sure it is real lambskin like this  @lemieuxproductsofficial one. Fake stuff isnt good! ","views":156300},{"id":"7522977104112143638","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7522977104112143638","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Sometimes it’s not just about *your* weight. It’s about the rest of the stuff you ask your horse to carry, it’s about their *ideal* weight… and also their age and fitness. As well as rider fitness and balance. So many variables. But a good place to start is to weight yourself with all your tack. All of it. And get your horse weighed and find out their ideal weight too. And consider… how fit and strong are they? And of course saddle fit! #riderweight #horsesoftiktok #horsegirl #horseriding  #horsewelfare #fit4welfare. ","views":52300},{"id":"7557775519836802327","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7557775519836802327","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"He is the one. #dirtybertie #bestboy #overheightconnie #connemarahorse ","views":58000},{"id":"7685900960022973728","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7685900960022973728","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"White stuff on saddles doesn’t always mean they’re mouldy. This is leather ‘bloom’ and can happen when the leather gets hot and then cold. The natural oils come out and sit on the surface. It feels waxy. And is often worse on buffalo leather like this. Quick fix? Zap it with the hairdryer for five seconds and boom it’s gone. Once it’s melted, just wipe away or rub it in. Personally I am a rubber inner. Don’t overdo the heat though. Leather doesn’t like it. ","views":1193},{"id":"7678413082359598358","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7678413082359598358","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Stop worrying about being crap at something. #dolly #dollyquotes #leatherwork #saddlery ","views":1326},{"id":"7671397659902528790","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7671397659902528790","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"There is nothing better than cantering through the woods at @LittleLodgeFarm  ","views":601},{"id":"7647268608560647446","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7647268608560647446","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"It’s ok. I only have geldings. ","views":1349},{"id":"7646480470342978838","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7646480470342978838","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Is there anything better than cuddling your horse when you catch them having a snooze? Nope.  ","views":661},{"id":"7644816334890585366","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7644816334890585366","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Which are your faves? Because I seem to have accidentally become a one woman Celeris showroom and I love them all but I think my faves are 4. Or 5. Yeah 5. Oh I don’t know.  1️⃣ The eBay specials. Bought years ago. Too short. Too wide. Absolutely zero business fitting me properly. Did I still wear them like they were custom-made by angels? Yes. Yes I did. Should probably sell them. But won’t.  2️⃣ My daily boots. Fully fur lined. Basically my best friends at this point. If these boots ever leave me, I’ll need counselling. The first things I’d save in a fire. Sorry. Not sorry.  3️⃣ Competition boots. Super firm through the leg which is AMAZING for my hypermobile ankles because without them my lower leg flaps around like on of those inflatable tube man outside a dodgy car dealership. These actually keep me together and make me look vaguely elegant. I said ‘vaguely’, ok? 4️⃣ The polo boots. I genuinely thought I’d never love them as much as the Bia laced ones- but I felt like I needed to try them. Reader… I was an idiot. These were comfy from the second I put them on. No breaking in. No suffering. No ‘beauty is pain’. Just immediate lush pink sparkly comfort.  5️⃣ These are just FILTHY levels of classiness (is that even a word?). The leather is so soft I’m scared to breathe near them in case I crease them. Put them on and it was like slipping into buttery little clouds for your legs. It is rude how comfy they are. Which would you choose? Every day I totally pinch myself that I get to be an ambassador for @celerisuk  because years ago I remember sitting with @pretty_stitched_company  looking at them all and DREAMING about owning a pair one day. And now I somehow have five. Five. This is what happens when someone with poor self control and a credit card pays a visit to Celeris HQ.","views":930},{"id":"7644323018252012822","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7644323018252012822","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Pink or brown? Or both? Maybe i should mix them up and wear one of each. After all, you only see one side at a time when I’m on a horse… #celeris #ridingboots #madetomeasureboots #HorseGirlEnergy ","views":1102},{"id":"7642481481448901891","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7642481481448901891","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"I was feeding COW PARSLEY. not hemlock. Cow parsley is absolutely fine for horses to eat. It looks similar to hemlock but it very different. It’s actually good for them. And it’s my horse’s fave snack. ","views":462},{"id":"7641344960100306199","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7641344960100306199","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"True story.  #asmr #horseasmr ","views":4935},{"id":"7640261817138187542","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@poppywebber/video/7640261817138187542","authorHandle":"poppywebber","description":"Saw others doing this trend with a dog. Tried it on my horse. 🤣","views":8129}],"warnings":["TikTok 创作者嵌入页的视频样本没有已核实的发布时间或最新顺序；本轮仅读取播放量，单条点赞和评论数未采集。"]},"biography":"Queen of Petrol Light Roulette.\nSaddle fitter. Entrepreneur. Horsey Gal."}],"emails":[],"websites":[{"url":"https://poppywebber.co.uk/","label":"Website","identityStatus":"channel_published"},{"url":"https://facebook.com/groups/tackroomchat","label":"FB Group","identityStatus":"channel_published"}],"profileSources":{"name":{"sourceUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChA8TK7yu4